--> !scheduled.contains(name)
run.specialize(mode) comes after another directive on run. specialize goes first: the copies it makes, one per variant, are what the directives after it schedule -- one variant's (`run[<Variant>].bind(...)`) or every variant's (`run.bind(...)`).
